 Downtown condos for corporate travel ($1,200-$1,800/month)\n- Multi-bedroom properties for student co-living ($1,800-$2,800/month)\n\n### Landlord Approach\n- Emphasize USC student and parent demand\n- Highlight state government travel needs\n- Offer longer lease terms (12-24 months)\n- Show professional management capabilities\n- Provide rent guarantee and insurance\n\n## Tax Obligations\n\n- **State Accommodations Tax**: 2%\n- **Local Accommodations Tax**: 2%\n- **South Carolina Sales Tax**: 6%\n- **Total**: 10% on gross rental income\n\n## Profitability Analysis\n\n**Example: 3BR Home Near USC**\n- Monthly Rent: $1,600\n- Average Nightly Rate: $160\n- Occupancy: 68%\n- Monthly Revenue: $3,264\n- Net Profit: $1,200-$1,600/month\n\n## Getting Started\n\nAccess Your Place provides complete acquisition and setup services for Columbia rental arbitrage operations. Our team handles licensing, furnishing, and launch for $2,500.\n\n**Contact**: hello@accessyourplace.com | Visit: deal.accessyourplace.com\n  	Complete guide to Columbia SC short-term rental licensing, co-living regulations, and rental arbitrage opportunities in 2025.	["columbia sc str license", "south carolina short term rental laws", "columbia vacation rental permit", "co-living columbia sc"]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	published	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2025-12-01 14:10:29.200313+00	2025-12-01 14:10:29.200313+00	2025-12-01 14:10:29.162+00	\N
