150a5276-6516-48c8-8f15-8d7ddc04c88e	Success_Team	Dispute Resolution	Dispute Resolution & Escalation	\n            <h4>Dispute Resolution Protocol</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the handling of investor complaints and dispute resolution.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Dispute Categories</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Level 1:</strong> Service delays, communication issues</li>\n              <li><strong>Level 2:</strong> Fee disputes, deal quality concerns</li>\n              <li><strong>Level 3:</strong> Refund requests, contract disputes</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Resolution Process</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Log dispute in the Disputes Tab with full details</li>\n              <li>Acknowledge receipt to investor within 4 hours</li>\n              <li>Investigate and gather all relevant documentation</li>\n              <li>Propose resolution within 48 hours</li>\n              <li>Escalate to management if unresolved after 5 business days</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>Refund Policy</h5>\n            <div class="alert-warning">\n              <strong>Non-Refundable Fees:</strong> Acquisition fees are non-refundable once the Acquisition Agreement has been signed and the property address has been revealed.\n            </div>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Deal falls through due to landlord rejection: Replacement property at no additional fee</li>\n              <li>Investor withdraws before address reveal: Full refund minus processing fee</li>\n              <li>Service quality issues: Case-by-case evaluation by Success Team</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Escalation Path</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Success Team Member → Success Team Lead</li>\n              <li>Success Team Lead → Operations Manager</li>\n              <li>Operations Manager → Executive Team</li>\n            </ol>\n          	3	f	2026-01-30 15:21:19.25952+00	2026-01-30 15:21:19.225+00	System	1	Initial creation
e9c6aadb-558d-4374-b4cb-4843c786257c	Success_Team	Onboarding	Discovery & Onboarding Bridge	\n            <h4>Discovery & Onboarding Bridge Protocol</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the initial investor consultation and account activation process.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Step 1: Initial Contact Response</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Respond to all new investor inquiries within 2 business hours</li>\n              <li>Use the "Welcome to AYP" email template for first contact</li>\n              <li>Schedule a discovery call within 48 hours of initial contact</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Step 2: Discovery Call Protocol</h5>\n            <div class="alert-warning">\n              <strong>$5,000 Capital Verification:</strong> During the initial AM consultation, verify the investor has minimum $5,000 liquid reserves to safely complete the investment cycle. This is non-negotiable.\n            </div>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Review investor's experience level and goals</li>\n              <li>Explain the AYP acquisition process and timeline</li>\n              <li>Discuss target markets and property preferences</li>\n              <li>Verify capital availability (minimum $5,000 liquid)</li>\n              <li>Set clear expectations about fees and timelines</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Step 3: Account Initiation</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Create investor account in the portal</li>\n              <li>Send welcome email with portal access credentials</li>\n              <li>Assign to appropriate Acquisition Manager based on target market</li>\n              <li>Schedule follow-up call within 1 week</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Step 4: Documentation</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Log all interactions in the CRM</li>\n              <li>Update investor profile with preferences and notes</li>\n              <li>Set automated follow-up reminders</li>\n            </ul>\n          	1	f	2026-01-30 15:21:19.033665+00	2026-01-30 15:21:18.93+00	System	1	Initial creation
35d81151-8c32-4884-a81f-bbe3d6b75b74	Acquisition_Manager	Landlord Outreach	Landlord Outreach Process	\n            <h4>Landlord Outreach & Relationship Building</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the process of contacting and building relationships with landlords.</p>\n            \n            <div class="alert-critical">\n              <strong>Ocean307 Protocol:</strong> Always lead with the company password "Ocean307" when contacting landlords to verify your identity as an AYP representative.\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>Initial Contact Protocol</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Research property and landlord background</li>\n              <li>Prepare talking points specific to the property</li>\n              <li>Make initial contact via phone (preferred) or email</li>\n              <li>Introduce AYP and the corporate housing model</li>\n              <li>Schedule follow-up meeting if interested</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>Key Talking Points</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Guaranteed rent payments (no vacancy risk)</li>\n              <li>Professional property care and maintenance</li>\n              <li>Corporate tenants with background checks</li>\n              <li>Long-term lease commitment (12+ months)</li>\n              <li>Single point of contact for all issues</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Follow-Up Schedule</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Day 1: Initial contact</li>\n              <li>Day 3: Follow-up if no response</li>\n              <li>Day 7: Second follow-up</li>\n              <li>Day 14: Final follow-up before moving on</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Documentation</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Log all contacts in CRM immediately</li>\n              <li>Record landlord preferences and concerns</li>\n              <li>Update deal status after each interaction</li>\n            </ul>\n          	2	f	2026-01-30 15:21:19.590308+00	2026-01-30 15:21:19.552+00	System	1	Initial creation
9c208458-a338-413c-9458-edb9bcda3f3f	Acquisition_Manager	Property Research	Property Research Protocol	\n            <h4>Property Research & Market Analysis Protocol</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the research and validation process for potential acquisition properties.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Market Research Tools</h5>\n            <div class="alert-info">\n              <strong>Required Data Sources:</strong> Cross-reference AirDNA, Rabbu, Mashvisor, and AllTheRooms for ADR, ARR, and occupancy validation.\n            </div>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>AirDNA:</strong> Primary source for ADR and occupancy rates</li>\n              <li><strong>Rabbu:</strong> Revenue projections and market trends</li>\n              <li><strong>Mashvisor:</strong> Neighborhood analysis and comparables</li>\n              <li><strong>AllTheRooms:</strong> Supply and demand metrics</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Property Evaluation Criteria</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Minimum projected monthly revenue: 2x monthly rent</li>\n              <li>Occupancy rate target: 65% or higher</li>\n              <li>ADR must support profitability after expenses</li>\n              <li>Location within 15 minutes of key attractions/business centers</li>\n              <li>Property condition suitable for furnished rental</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Documentation Requirements</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Screenshot market data from all four sources</li>\n              <li>Create property analysis spreadsheet</li>\n              <li>Document comparable listings in the area</li>\n              <li>Note any regulatory considerations (HOA, STR permits)</li>\n              <li>Upload all documentation to deal record</li>\n            </ol>\n          	1	f	2026-01-30 15:21:19.482097+00	2026-01-30 15:21:19.438+00	System	1	Initial creation
cf9aa7d2-906c-40fb-b82a-2ad69647ad59	Acquisition_Manager	Success Team Handoff	Success Team Handoff Protocol	\n            <h4>Success Team Handoff Protocol</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the transition of deals from Acquisition to Success Team.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Handoff Checklist</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Property analysis complete with all market data</li>\n              <li>Landlord approval documented</li>\n              <li>Lease terms finalized</li>\n              <li>Property photos uploaded (minimum 10)</li>\n              <li>Setup cost estimate prepared</li>\n              <li>Investor matched and notified</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Documentation Requirements</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Complete deal summary in CRM</li>\n              <li>Upload all landlord communications</li>\n              <li>Document any special terms or conditions</li>\n              <li>Note landlord preferences and concerns</li>\n              <li>Include timeline expectations</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>Handoff Meeting</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Schedule 15-minute handoff call with Success Team</li>\n              <li>Review all deal details and documentation</li>\n              <li>Discuss any potential issues or concerns</li>\n              <li>Confirm next steps and responsibilities</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Post-Handoff Support</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Remain available for landlord questions during application</li>\n              <li>Assist with any negotiation issues that arise</li>\n              <li>Support Success Team through lease signing</li>\n            </ul>\n          	4	f	2026-01-30 15:21:19.906003+00	2026-01-30 15:21:19.867+00	System	1	Initial creation
430eb60b-80ff-498b-932f-6f5d1f10d74d	Setup_Manager	Quality Inspection	Quality Inspection Standards	\n            <h4>Quality Inspection & Final Walkthrough</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the final inspection process before property launch.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Inspection Checklist</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Cleanliness:</strong> All surfaces spotless, no dust or debris</li>\n              <li><strong>Functionality:</strong> All appliances, fixtures, and systems working</li>\n              <li><strong>Completeness:</strong> All furniture and supplies in place</li>\n              <li><strong>Safety:</strong> Smoke detectors, fire extinguisher, first aid kit</li>\n              <li><strong>Aesthetics:</strong> Consistent design, no visible damage</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Photography Requirements</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Minimum 20 high-quality photos</li>\n              <li>Natural lighting preferred</li>\n              <li>Wide-angle shots of each room</li>\n              <li>Detail shots of amenities and features</li>\n              <li>Exterior and building common areas</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Issue Resolution</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Document any issues found during inspection</li>\n              <li>Prioritize by severity (critical, moderate, minor)</li>\n              <li>Assign resolution tasks with deadlines</li>\n              <li>Re-inspect after corrections made</li>\n              <li>Sign off only when all issues resolved</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>Launch Approval</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>All inspection items must pass</li>\n              <li>Photography approved by Success Team</li>\n              <li>Listing copy reviewed and approved</li>\n              <li>Smart lock and WiFi tested</li>\n              <li>Welcome guide and house manual in place</li>\n            </ul>\n          	3	f	2026-01-30 15:21:20.332299+00	2026-01-30 15:21:20.275+00	System	1	Initial creation
b03b5bac-d465-4bd7-b265-3ab2ca9fdb0a	Setup_Manager	Vendor Management	Vendor Management Protocol	\n            <h4>Vendor Management & Coordination</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the management of vendors and service providers.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Vendor Categories</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Cleaning:</strong> Deep cleaning, turnover cleaning</li>\n              <li><strong>Maintenance:</strong> Repairs, handyman services</li>\n              <li><strong>Delivery:</strong> Furniture delivery and assembly</li>\n              <li><strong>Photography:</strong> Professional property photography</li>\n              <li><strong>Specialty:</strong> Locksmith, HVAC, plumbing</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Vendor Onboarding</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Verify business license and insurance</li>\n              <li>Check references and reviews</li>\n              <li>Negotiate rates and terms</li>\n              <li>Add to approved vendor list</li>\n              <li>Provide AYP standards and expectations</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>Scheduling & Coordination</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Book vendors at least 48 hours in advance</li>\n              <li>Confirm appointments 24 hours before</li>\n              <li>Provide property access instructions</li>\n              <li>Follow up after service completion</li>\n              <li>Document any issues or feedback</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Quality Control</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Inspect work before signing off</li>\n              <li>Rate vendor performance after each job</li>\n              <li>Address issues immediately with vendor</li>\n              <li>Remove underperforming vendors from list</li>\n            </ul>\n          	4	f	2026-01-30 15:21:20.442947+00	2026-01-30 15:21:20.406+00	System	1	Initial creation
e22bb704-5d12-47be-8243-cf106af1e4f9	Cross_Team	Compliance	Platform Security & Ocean307 Protocol	\n            <h4>Platform Security & Identity Verification</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs security protocols and identity verification.</p>\n            \n            <div class="alert-critical">\n              <strong>Ocean307 Protocol:</strong> This is the company password used to verify AYP representative identity when contacting landlords or partners. Always lead with this password in initial communications.\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>When to Use Ocean307</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>First contact with new landlords</li>\n              <li>Calling property management companies</li>\n              <li>Verifying identity to partners or vendors</li>\n              <li>When asked to confirm AYP affiliation</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Account Security</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Never share login credentials</li>\n              <li>Use strong, unique passwords</li>\n              <li>Log out when leaving workstation</li>\n              <li>Report suspicious activity immediately</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Data Protection</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Investor data is confidential</li>\n              <li>Property addresses protected until half-funded</li>\n              <li>Landlord contacts never shared with investors</li>\n              <li>All deal information is proprietary</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Breach Response</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Report immediately to Success Team</li>\n              <li>Document the incident</li>\n              <li>Change affected passwords</li>\n              <li>Notify affected parties as directed</li>\n            </ol>\n          	3	f	2026-01-30 15:21:20.788815+00	2026-01-30 15:21:20.754+00	System	1	Initial creation
1bb072c9-2306-454f-b926-4afaa938a5a0	Cross_Team	Compliance	Confidentiality & Information Protection	\n            <h4>Confidentiality & Information Protection Standards</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the protection of confidential information.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Confidential Information Categories</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Investor Data:</strong> Personal information, financial details, preferences</li>\n              <li><strong>Deal Information:</strong> Property addresses, terms, pricing</li>\n              <li><strong>Landlord Contacts:</strong> Names, phone numbers, email addresses</li>\n              <li><strong>Business Operations:</strong> SOPs, strategies, vendor relationships</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Information Handling</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Access only information needed for your role</li>\n              <li>Store sensitive data only in approved systems</li>\n              <li>Never email confidential information externally</li>\n              <li>Shred physical documents when no longer needed</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <div class="alert-warning">\n              <strong>Half-Funded Rule:</strong> Full property addresses are only disclosed after 50% of the acquisition fee is funded or the investor has closed a prior deal.\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>Non-Disclosure Requirements</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>All staff sign NDA upon hiring</li>\n              <li>Confidentiality obligations continue after employment</li>\n              <li>Violations may result in termination and legal action</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Third-Party Sharing</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Written consent required for investor data sharing</li>\n              <li>Vendors receive only necessary information</li>\n              <li>Partners sign confidentiality agreements</li>\n            