730a5ab6-a5c9-4b47-9cd4-3abec236e1ef	Success_Team	Compliance	Credit & Integrity Standards	\n            <h4>YP Credits Policy & Platform Integrity</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the management of investor credits and platform security protocols.</p>\n            \n            <h5>YP Credits Management</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Credits are earned through referrals ($500 per successful referral)</li>\n              <li>Credits can only be applied to AYP Approved Deals</li>\n              <li>Credits have no cash value and cannot be transferred</li>\n              <li>Maximum credit application per deal: 50% of acquisition fee</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Credit Issuance Process</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Verify referral has completed their first acquisition</li>\n              <li>Issue credit to referring investor's account</li>\n              <li>Send notification email with credit balance update</li>\n              <li>Log transaction in credit ledger</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <div class="alert-critical">\n              <strong>Ocean307 Security Protocol:</strong> When contacting landlords or partners, always lead with the company password "Ocean307" to verify AYP representative identity. This protects our landlord relationships and prevents unauthorized contact.\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>Privacy Standards</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Never share investor information with third parties without consent</li>\n              <li>Property addresses are confidential until 50% fee funded</li>\n              <li>All deal information is proprietary and protected</li>\n              <li>Landlord contacts are never shared with investors directly</li>\n            </ul>\n          	2	f	2026-01-30 15:21:19.154381+00	2026-01-30 15:21:19.118+00	System	1	Initial creation
673190d2-aefb-4852-a966-6a318a0a5380	Success_Team	Onboarding	standard deal listing protocol	STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE: DEAL LISTING PROTOCOL\nDepartment: Success Team | Role: Success Manager\nSystem: Staff Admin Dashboard -> Deal Flow Tab\nSecurity Clearance: Admin/Success Team Only\nCompliance Password: Ocean307\nI. THE LISTING OBJECTIVE\nAs a Success Manager, your role in the "Deal Flow" is to verify, audit, and publish opportunities that our Acquisition Team sources. You are the final quality control gate before an investor sees a deal.\nYour Goal: Create a compelling, data-backed listing that hides the specific identity of the property (to protect the deal) while giving the investor enough "Foundation of Truth" data to make a decision.\nII. LISTING WORKFLOW (STEP-BY-STEP)\nStep 1: Access the Deal Flow Portal\n* Log in to the Staff Admin Dashboard.\n* Navigate to the "Deal Flow" tab on the left sidebar.\n* Click the green "Add New Deal" button.\nStep 2: The "Blind" Address Protocol\n* Internal Address Field: You must enter the actual address of the building so our system can track it.\n* Input for this Deal: 1704 N 17th St, Tampa, FL 33605\n* Note: The system automatically hides this from public view until a client purchases.\n* Public Title: Do NOT use the building name (e.g., "Miles at Ybor").\n* Format: [Unit Type] - [Neighborhood] - [Key Feature]\n* Input for Studio: Luxury Studio - Historic Ybor City - Walkable & Modern\n* Input for 3-Bed: 3-Bedroom Executive Suite - Ybor City - Co-Living & STR Ready\nStep 3: The Photo Integrity Standard\nWe must protect our exclusive partnerships. Never reveal the building identity in public photos.\n* Action: Go to the community website (provided by the Acquisition Manager) and download high-res photos.\n* The Filter:\n* ✅ DO upload: Interior living spaces, kitchens, bathrooms, generic bedroom shots.\n* ❌ DO NOT upload: Exterior building signs, lobby photos with logos, "Amenities" pages that show the pool or gym if they reveal the building identity.\n* Instruction for this Deal: Navigate to milesatybor.com/gallery. Strip only the interior apartment photos. Do not use photos of the exterior signage.\nStep 4: Performance Data Entry (The "Foundation of Truth")\nYou will audit the numbers provided by the Acquisition Manager. We publish numbers based on Top Tier Performance potential.\nA. STUDIO LISTING INPUTS:\n* Acquisition Fee: $2,825\n* Monthly Rent: $1,675 (Utilities Included)\n* Projected Monthly Revenue (Avg): $4,100\n* Occupancy Rate: 68% (Slow) / 81% (Peak)\n* ADR (Average Daily Rate): $145 (Slow) / $195 (Peak)\n* Deposit Requirement: 1 Month Rent (Subject to screening)\nB. 3-BEDROOM LISTING INPUTS:\n* Acquisition Fee: $2,825\n* Monthly Rent: $3,000 (Utilities Included)\n* Projected Monthly Revenue: $6,225\n* ADR: $325 - $385\n* Co-Living Strategy: Yes ($1,500/room -> $4,500 - $6,000 Revenue)\nIII. THE DEAL DESCRIPTION (COPYWRITING)\nCopy and paste the following description into the "Deal Description" text box. This copy is optimized for investor conversion.\nCopy for Studio Listing:\nHeadline: High-Velocity Short-Term Rental in the Heart of Ybor\nThis is a rare opportunity to secure a fully furnished luxury studio in one of Tampa’s most culturally vibrant and walkable districts. Located steps from the legendary dining and nightlife of Ybor City and just minutes from Downtown Tampa and the Riverwalk, this unit is perfectly positioned for high-occupancy short-term rental traffic.\nWhy This Deal Wins:\n* All-Inclusive Lease: Rent includes utilities, maximizing your cash flow margins.\n* Prime Location: Highly desirable for tourists and business travelers alike.\n* Turn-Key Potential: Exclusive partnership allows for immediate Corporate Lease compliance.\n* Performance: With peak ADRs hitting $195+, this unit is designed for an investor looking for a reliable, high-traffic asset.\nCopy for 3-Bedroom Listing:\nHeadline: Massive Cash Flow Potential - STR or Co-Living Powerhouse\nScale your portfolio instantly with this massive 3-Bedroom Executive Suite. This unique floor plan offers dual-strategy potential: operate it as a high-end Short-Term Rental for families and groups, or leverage the Co-Living model by renting individual rooms to traveling professionals for maximum stability.\nThe Strategy:\n* Co-Living Ready: At $1,500 per room, this unit can generate $4,500 - $6,000/mo with long-term stability.\n* Group Travel STR: With an ADR of $325-$385, this is a top-tier choice for groups visiting Tampa’s historic district.\n* Exclusive Access: Secured through our direct partnership, bypassing standard waitlists.\n* Walkability: Guests are immersed in the Ybor experience—dining, history, and transit are at the doorstep.\n	0	f	2026-02-01 18:06:07.125635+00	2026-02-01 18:06:07.049+00	Cynthia KossyKoss	1	Initial creation
d6d99cc1-2994-4bf2-8ae9-212a9a03e121	Setup_Manager	Setup Workflow	Setup Fee Structure & Commission Rules	<h4>Setup Fee Structure & Commission Rules</h4><p>This SOP details all fees, payment timing, and commission calculations for the setup workflow.</p><h5>Fee Schedule</h5><table><tr><th>Fee</th><th>Amount</th><th>When Collected</th><th>Who Pays</th></tr><tr><td>Setup Administration Fee</td><td>$2,500 (can vary)</td><td>Phase 1 - to lock in service or when ready</td><td>Operator</td></tr><tr><td>Setup Logistics Fee (DFY only)</td><td>$3,350</td><td>Phase 4 - before Pro assignment</td><td>Operator</td></tr><tr><td>Furniture & Supply Fee</td><td>Variable (based on sourcing)</td><td>Phase 5 - after spreadsheet approval</td><td>Operator</td></tr></table><h5>Commission Structure</h5><ul><li><strong>Setup Manager Commission:</strong> 15% of the Admin Fee</li><li><strong>Trigger:</strong> Automatically queued upon Admin Fee payment recording</li><li><strong>Payout Schedule:</strong> Next Friday after payment (aligns with company payroll)</li><li><strong>Example:</strong> $2,500 admin fee = $375 commission, paid on the following Friday</li></ul><h5>Setup Pro Compensation</h5><ul><li><strong>Flat Fee:</strong> $1,200 per job</li><li><strong>Trigger:</strong> Disbursed after Pro signs the Independent Contractor Agreement</li><li><strong>Applies to:</strong> DFY packages only</li></ul><div class='alert-warning'><strong>Important:</strong> All fees must be recorded in the portal before advancing to the next phase. Never advance a phase without confirming payment has been received and logged.</div><h5>DIY vs DFY Fee Comparison</h5><p><strong>DIY Package:</strong></p><ul><li>Admin Fee: $2,500</li><li>Furniture & Supply Fee: Variable</li><li>Total: ~$2,500 + furniture costs</li></ul><p><strong>DFY Package:</strong></p><ul><li>Admin Fee: $2,500</li><li>Logistics Fee: $3,350</li><li>Furniture & Supply Fee: Variable</li><li>Setup Pro Fee: $1,200 (paid by company)</li><li>Total: ~$5,850 + furniture costs</li></ul>	2	f	2026-03-05 17:48:13.790328+00	2026-03-05 17:48:13.743+00	System	1	Initial creation
5637bb49-605f-4203-b83c-512432bf7621	Setup_Manager	Setup Workflow	Setup Workflow - Complete 8-Phase Process	<h4>Setup Workflow: Complete 8-Phase Process</h4><p>This SOP documents the full end-to-end setup workflow from property selection through final handover. All Setup Managers must follow this process for every project.</p><h5>Phase 1: Acquisition & Initial Payment</h5><ul><li><strong>Property Selection:</strong> The Operator selects a property with the Acquisition team.</li><li><strong>Admin Fee Payment:</strong> The Operator pays the Setup Administration fee (typically $2,500, but can vary). This can be paid immediately to lock in the service or when they are ready for setup.</li><li><strong>Manager Commission Trigger:</strong> Upon successful payment of the Administration Fee, the portal queues the Setup Manager's 15% commission to be paid out on the following Friday (aligning with company payroll).</li></ul><div class='alert-info'><strong>Key Rule:</strong> The admin fee must be recorded in the portal before advancing to Phase 2. The commission is automatically calculated at 15% and queued for the next Friday payout.</div><h5>Phase 2: Consultation & Pre-Intake</h5><ul><li><strong>Manager Assignment:</strong> The portal assigns a Setup Manager to the Operator.</li><li><strong>Consultation Call:</strong> The Setup Manager speaks with the Operator to explain the process and determine if they want the 'Done For You' (DFY) or 'Do It Yourself' (DIY) package.</li><li><strong>Recap Communication:</strong> The Setup Manager triggers the appropriate Recap Template (DFY or DIY) to be sent as an email or portal message. This outlines the process, fee structure, and includes the link to the Intake Form.</li></ul><div class='alert-warning'><strong>DFY vs DIY:</strong> This decision affects the entire workflow. DIY packages skip Phases 4, 6, and 7 (logistics, purchasing/travel, and on-site setup). Confirm the package type before sending the recap.</div><h5>Phase 3: Intake Form & Service Agreement</h5><ul><li><strong>Intake Form Submission:</strong> The Operator fills out the Intake Form in their portal.</li><li><strong>Agreement Generation:</strong> The Setup Manager uses the intake data to generate the Setup Service Agreement detailing the chosen services and fees.</li><li><strong>Sign-Off:</strong> The Operator reviews, signs, and returns the agreement via the portal.</li></ul><h5>Phase 4: Logistics & Team Activation (DFY Only)</h5><div class='alert-info'><strong>DIY Note:</strong> If the Operator chose DIY, this phase is skipped entirely. Move directly to Phase 5.</div><ul><li><strong>Logistics Payment:</strong> The Operator pays the $3,350 Setup Logistics Fee via the portal.</li><li><strong>Pro Assignment & Contract:</strong> The Setup Manager assigns a Setup Pro. The portal generates a secure, external link to the Independent Contractor Agreement and emails it to the Pro.</li><li><strong>Pro Signature & Payout:</strong> The Pro signs the agreement via the external link and is disbursed their $1,200 flat fee for the job.</li></ul><h5>Phase 5: Product Sourcing & Spreadsheet Approval</h5><ul><li><strong>Sourcing (24-48 Hours):</strong> The Setup Manager sources items on Amazon.</li><li><strong>Spreadsheet Population:</strong> The Manager populates the portal's integrated Sourcing Spreadsheet.</li><li><strong>Spreadsheet Access Routing:</strong><ul><li><strong>Operator View:</strong> Can view the spreadsheet inside their portal (sees items, photos, delivery status, and only the grand total Furniture & Supply Fee at the bottom).</li><li><strong>Pro View:</strong> The portal generates an external link emailed to the Pro so they can access the spreadsheet to view items, photos, and update the delivery/placement status checkboxes later.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Final Payment:</strong> Once the Operator approves the spreadsheet in the portal, they pay the finalized Furniture & Supply Fee.</li></ul><h5>Phase 6: Purchasing & Travel Logistics (DFY Only)</h5><div class='alert-info'><strong>DIY Note:</strong> If DIY, this phase is skipped. The Operator handles their own purchasing.</div><ul><li><strong>Purchasing:</strong> The Setup Manager purchases all approved items.</li><li><strong>Flight Booking:</strong> The Manager identifies the earliest item delivery date and books the Setup Pro's flight to arrive on that exact day.</li></ul><h5>Phase 7: On-Site Setup & Live Tracking (7-14 Business Days, DFY Only)</h5><div class='alert-info'><strong>DIY Note:</strong> If DIY, this phase is skipped.</div><ul><li><strong>Pro Arrival & Maintenance Check:</strong> The Pro arrives. Before unboxing anything, the Pro clicks the external link provided by the portal to access the mobile-friendly 'Maintenance Inventory Form.' They walk the property, document its condition, and submit the form. This automatically routes back to the Setup Manager to forward to the property's maintenance team.</li><li><strong>Vendor Management:</strong><ul><li><strong>Setup Manager:</strong> Handles all booking, scheduling, and management of on-site appointments (e.g., Wi-Fi installation, utility setups).</li><li><strong>Setup Pro:</strong> Acts as the on-site point of contact to unlock the door, let vendors in, and remain present while the work is completed.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Delivery Verification (Video):</strong> As items arrive, the Setup Manager initiates a video call with the Pro to visually verify the exact items dropped off.</li><li><strong>Live Inventory Tracking:</strong> The Pro uses their external spreadsheet link to check off items as they are delivered and placed. The Operator and Manager watch these updates live.</li></ul><h5>Phase 8: Clean-up, Media Capture, & Final Handover</h5><ul><li><strong>Clean-up:</strong> The Pro thoroughly cleans the property, removing all boxes, trash, and debris.</li><li><strong>Media Capture:</strong> The Pro turns on all lights, takes professional photos, and records a continuous video walkthrough (ensuring they are not visible in the footage).</li><li><strong>Media Upload:</strong> The Pro uploads the photos and videos via an external portal link.</li><li><strong>Manager Approval:</strong> The Setup Manager reviews and approves the media in the portal.</li><li><strong>Departure:</strong> The Manager marks the setup as complete and prepares the Pro's return flight.</li><li><strong>Final Delivery:</strong> The portal sends the final furnished photos and video walkthrough to the Operator, officially closing the job.</li></ul><div class='alert-critical'><strong>Completion Checklist:</strong> Before marking a project complete, verify: (1) All media approved, (2) Final photos/video sent to Operator, (3) All payments recorded, (4) Pro return flight arranged (DFY), (5) Maintenance form submitted and forwarded.</div>	1	f	2026-03-05 17:48:00.743697+00	2026-03-05 17:48:00.697+00	System	1	Initial creation
a01d3466-a98f-4171-9a0e-3c635e09bb0c	Success_Team	Compliance	IV. Credit & Integrity Standards	<h4>Credit & Integrity Standards</h4>\n<h5>YP Credits</h5>\n<p>Credits are issued for the <strong>full acquisition fee</strong> if:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A landlord withdraws</li>\n<li>An application is denied through no fault of the client</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Credit Utilization</h5>\n<p>Credits apply to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>YP-approved acquisitions</li>\n<li>Setup administration</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Credits NEVER apply to:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Logistics costs</li>\n<li>Third-party fees</li>\n<li>Furniture costs</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Security Protocol</h5>\n<p>All staff must lead with the password <strong>"Ocean307"</strong> when contacting any community or landlord partner.</p>\n<h5>Privacy</h5>\n<p>ST ensures that Buyer and Seller identities remain confidential throughout the transaction to protect the network.</p>\n<div class="alert-critical">\n<strong>Critical:</strong> Never disclose investor or landlord personal information to third parties without explicit written consent.\n</div>	4	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
038bc937-b76e-46a5-af7a-1896b9419ac8	Success_Team	Penny AI	Penny AI Overview & Scoring System	\n            <h4>Penny AI: Your AI-Powered Deal Intelligence System</h4>\n            <p>Penny AI is Access Your Place's proprietary artificial intelligence system designed to provide data-driven deal scoring, market analysis, and investment recommendations. This SOP provides a comprehensive overview of Penny's capabilities and the scoring methodology.</p>\n            \n            <h5>What is Penny AI?</h5>\n            <p>Penny is an AI Success Manager that combines machine learning algorithms with real-time market data to:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Score potential deals on a 0-100 scale</li>\n              <li>Analyze market conditions across 23 supported markets</li>\n              <li>Provide revenue projections for STR, Co-living, and MTR strategies</li>\n              <li>Identify risks and opportunities for each property</li>\n              <li>Match investors with deals based on their preferences</li>\n              <li>Answer investor questions with SOP-verified responses</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>The Penny Score (0-100)</h5>\n            <div class="alert-info">\n              <strong>Score Ranges:</strong><br/>\n              • <strong>80-100 (Excellent):</strong> Strong buy recommendation - exceptional opportunity<br/>\n              • <strong>60-79 (Good):</strong> Buy recommendation - solid investment potential<br/>\n              • <strong>40-59 (Fair):</strong> Hold/Review - needs additional analysis<br/>\n              • <strong>0-39 (Poor):</strong> Avoid - significant risks identified\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>Scoring Components (6 Factors)</h5>\n            <p>Penny evaluates each property across six key dimensions:</p>\n            <ol>\n              <li><strong>Market Score (20%):</strong> Overall market health, demand trends, and growth potential</li>\n              <li><strong>Financial Score (25%):</strong> Revenue potential, profit margins, and ROI projections</li>\n              <li><strong>Regulation Score (15%):</strong> STR permit requirements, zoning compliance, and regulatory risk</li>\n              <li><strong>Competition Score (15%):</strong> Market saturation, competitor analysis, and differentiation potential</li>\n              <li><strong>Seasonality Score (15%):</strong> Demand patterns, peak/slow season analysis, and revenue stability</li>\n              <li><strong>Location Score (10%):</strong> Proximity to attractions, accessibility, and neighborhood quality</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>Data Sources</h5>\n            <p>Penny aggregates data from multiple sources to ensure accuracy:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Market data snapshots (updated weekly)</li>\n              <li>Seasonality calendar (23 markets, 12 months)</li>\n              <li>Historical performance data from AYP portfolio</li>\n              <li>Machine learning feedback from actual property performance</li>\n              <li>Real-time property listings and comparables</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Recommendation Types</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Strong Buy:</strong> Score 80+ with high confidence - prioritize this deal</li>\n              <li><strong>Buy:</strong> Score 60-79 - solid opportunity worth pursuing</li>\n              <li><strong>Hold:</strong> Score 40-59 - needs additional due diligence</li>\n              <li><strong>Needs Review:</strong> Score 40-59 with specific concerns flagged</li>\n              <li><strong>Avoid:</strong> Score below 40 - significant risks outweigh potential</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <div class="alert-warning">\n              <strong>Important:</strong> Penny scores are advisory tools, not guarantees. All deals should still undergo human review and due diligence. Scores below 40 are automatically flagged for Success Team review.\n            </div>\n          	1	f	2026-02-01 19:04:20.363871+00	2026-02-01 19:04:20.322+00	System	1	Initial creation - Penny AI SOPs
6b03c081-578f-41fe-a41f-d7fa5122cc59	Success_Team	Penny AI	Penny AI Troubleshooting Guide	\n            <h4>Troubleshooting Common Penny AI Issues</h4>\n            <p>This guide helps resolve common issues encountered when using Penny AI.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Scoring Issues</h5>\n            \n            <h5>1. Score Not Generating</h5>\n            <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> "No analysis available" or loading indefinitely</p>\n            <p><strong>Solutions:</strong></p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Verify property has required fields (address, city, state, bedrooms, rent)</li>\n              <li>Check if market is in supported list (23 markets)</li>\n              <li>Click "Generate Analysis" or "Refresh" button</li>\n              <li>Clear browser cache and retry</li>\n              <li>If persistent, report to tech team</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>2. Score Seems Incorrect</h5>\n            <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Score doesn't match your market knowledge</p>\n            <p><strong>Solutions:</strong></p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Review component scores to identify the issue</li>\n              <li>Verify property data is accurate and complete</li>\n              <li>Check if market data is current (weekly refresh)</li>\n              <li>Consider if unique factors aren't captured by algorithm</li>\n              <li>Submit feedback through ML dashboard</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>3. Score Expired</h5>\n            <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Score shows old date or "expired" warning</p>\n            <p><strong>Solutions:</strong></p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Click refresh button to generate new score</li>\n              <li>Scores expire after 7 days automatically</li>\n              <li>Always refresh before presenting to investors</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Chat Issues</h5>\n            \n            <h5>4. Penny Not Responding</h5>\n            <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Chat shows loading indefinitely</p>\n            <p><strong>Solutions:</strong></p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Check internet connection</li>\n              <li>Refresh the page</li>\n              <li>Try a simpler question first</li>\n              <li>Clear conversation and start new chat</li>\n              <li>Report if issue persists for 5+ minutes</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>5. Penny Gives Incorrect Information</h5>\n            <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Response contains factual errors</p>\n            <p><strong>Solutions:</strong></p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Do not share incorrect info with investors</li>\n              <li>Verify information through other sources</li>\n              <li>Report the error with screenshot</li>\n              <li>Provide correct information to investor directly</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>6. Penny Doesn't Understand Question</h5>\n            <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Response is off-topic or generic</p>\n            <p><strong>Solutions:</strong></p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Rephrase question more specifically</li>\n              <li>Include market name and property type</li>\n              <li>Break complex questions into parts</li>\n              <li>Use suggested questions as templates</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Data Issues</h5>\n            \n            <h5>7. Market Data Missing</h5>\n            <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> "No market data available" message</p>\n            <p><strong>Solutions:</strong></p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Verify market is in supported list</li>\n              <li>Check spelling of city/market name</li>\n              <li>Report missing market data to tech team</li>\n              <li>Use closest comparable market temporarily</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>8. Seasonality Data Incorrect</h5>\n            <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Peak season info doesn't match reality</p>\n            <p><strong>Solutions:</strong></p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Submit correction through feedback system</li>\n              <li>Document the discrepancy with evidence</li>\n              <li>Use your market knowledge to advise investors</li>\n              <li>Flag for data team review</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Technical Issues</h5>\n            \n            <h5>9. Slow Performance</h5>\n            <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Scoring takes more than 30 seconds</p>\n            <p><strong>Solutions:</strong></p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Check internet connection speed</li>\n              <li>Avoid batch scoring during peak hours</li>\n              <li>Report consistent slowness to tech team</li>\n              <li>Try again during off-peak hours</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>10. Feature Not Working</h5>\n            <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Button doesn't respond, feature unavailable</p>\n            <p><strong>Solutions:</strong></p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Refresh the page</li>\n              <li>Clear browser cache</li>\n              <li>Try different browser</li>\n              <li>Check if feature requires specific permissions</li>\n              <li>Report with screenshot and steps to reproduce</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Escalation Path</h5>\n            <div class="alert-info">\n              <strong>When to Escalate:</strong><br/>\n              1. Issue persists after troubleshooting<br/>\n              2. Multiple users report same issue<br/>\n              3. Issue affects investor-facing features<br/>\n              4. Data accuracy concerns<br/><br/>\n              <strong>Escalate to:</strong> Tech Team via #penny-support channel\n            </div>\n          	7	f	2026-02-01 19:04:21.263998+00	2026-02-01 19:04:21.227+00	System	1	Initial creation - Penny AI SOPs
849b016a-ce3f-4aa2-8c19-c9b9744d8657	Success_Team	Penny AI	Penny AI Features & Capabilities	\n            <h4>Complete Feature Reference: Penny AI Capabilities</h4>\n            <p>This comprehensive guide covers all Penny AI features available to the Success Team.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Core Features</h5>\n            \n            <h5>1. Deal Scoring Engine</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Automatic Scoring:</strong> New properties are scored upon creation</li>\n              <li><strong>On-Demand Refresh:</strong> Manual re-scoring with latest market data</li>\n              <li><strong>Batch Scoring:</strong> Score multiple properties simultaneously</li>\n              <li><strong>Score History:</strong> Track how scores change over time</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>2. Revenue Projections</h5>\n            <p>Penny provides projections for three operation strategies:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Short-Term Rental (STR):</strong>\n                <ul>\n                  <li>Estimated ADR (Average Daily Rate)</li>\n                  <li>Projected occupancy percentage</li>\n                  <li>Monthly and annual revenue estimates</li>\n                  <li>Profit after expenses</li>\n                </ul>\n              </li>\n              <li><strong>Co-Living:</strong>\n                <ul>\n                  <li>Number of rentable rooms</li>\n                  <li>Average room rate</li>\n                  <li>Occupancy projections</li>\n                  <li>Monthly revenue per room</li>\n                </ul>\n              </li>\n              <li><strong>Mid-Term Rental (MTR):</strong>\n                <ul>\n                  <li>Monthly rental rate</li>\n                  <li>Expected occupancy</li>\n                  <li>Annual revenue projection</li>\n                </ul>\n              </li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>3. Market Intelligence</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Market Trend Analysis:</strong> Booming, Growing, Stable, or Declining</li>\n              <li><strong>Demand Drivers:</strong> Key factors driving market demand</li>\n              <li><strong>Peak Season Identification:</strong> Best months for revenue</li>\n              <li><strong>Competition Analysis:</strong> Market saturation levels</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>4. Risk Assessment</h5>\n            <p>Penny identifies and categorizes risks:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Regulatory Risks:</strong> Permit requirements, zoning issues</li>\n              <li><strong>Market Risks:</strong> Oversaturation, declining demand</li>\n              <li><strong>Financial Risks:</strong> High rent-to-revenue ratio, thin margins</li>\n              <li><strong>Operational Risks:</strong> Property condition, location challenges</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>5. Opportunity Identification</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Undervalued properties in growing markets</li>\n              <li>Properties suited for multiple strategies</li>\n              <li>Seasonal arbitrage opportunities</li>\n              <li>Emerging market entry points</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>6. Investor Chat Interface</h5>\n            <p>Penny serves as an AI assistant for investors:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Answers questions about markets and deals</li>\n              <li>Provides personalized recommendations</li>\n              <li>Explains scoring methodology</li>\n              <li>Offers strategy guidance</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>7. Deal Matching</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Matches investors to deals based on preferences</li>\n              <li>Considers budget, target markets, and risk tolerance</li>\n              <li>Sends automated notifications for matching deals</li>\n              <li>Tracks match history and conversion rates</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>8. Supported Markets (23 Total)</h5>\n            <div class="alert-info">\n              Austin, Nashville, Tampa, Orlando, Phoenix, Denver, Miami, Dallas, Atlanta, Jacksonville, Charlotte, San Antonio, Raleigh-Durham, Houston, Scottsdale, Panama City Beach, St Augustine, Myrtle Beach, Fayetteville, Birmingham, West Palm Beach, Albuquerque, Santa Fe\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>9. Seasonality Calendar</h5>\n            <p>Each market has monthly data including:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Demand level (Low, Medium, High, Peak)</li>\n              <li>ADR multiplier (0.7x - 1.5x baseline)</li>\n              <li>Expected occupancy adjustment</li>\n              <li>Major events affecting demand</li>\n              <li>Pricing recommendations</li>\n            </ul>\n          	3	f	2026-02-01 19:04:20.710827+00	2026-02-01 19:04:20.674+00	System	1	Initial creation - Penny AI SOPs
2c6b84c3-a32b-4f08-a6bb-e81fc9a98cd3	Success_Team	Penny AI	Team Responsibilities with AI Systems	\n            <h4>Staff Responsibilities When Working with Penny AI</h4>\n            <p>This SOP outlines the ethical and operational responsibilities of Success Team members when utilizing AI-powered tools.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Core Principles</h5>\n            \n            <h5>1. AI as a Tool, Not a Replacement</h5>\n            <div class="alert-critical">\n              <strong>Critical Understanding:</strong> Penny AI is a decision-support tool. It does NOT replace human judgment, due diligence, or professional responsibility. Every AI recommendation should be validated by staff before acting.\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>2. Transparency with Investors</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Always disclose that Penny is an AI system</li>\n              <li>Never present AI recommendations as human analysis</li>\n              <li>Explain that scores are algorithmically generated</li>\n              <li>Be honest about AI limitations</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>3. Data Accuracy Responsibility</h5>\n            <p>Staff must ensure data quality for accurate scoring:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Verify property details before scoring</li>\n              <li>Update incorrect information promptly</li>\n              <li>Report data discrepancies to tech team</li>\n              <li>Don't manipulate data to influence scores</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Operational Responsibilities</h5>\n            \n            <h5>1. Score Verification Protocol</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Review Penny's score before presenting to investors</li>\n              <li>Check that property data is current and accurate</li>\n              <li>Verify the score aligns with your market knowledge</li>\n              <li>Note any discrepancies for discussion</li>\n              <li>Refresh scores older than 7 days</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>2. Flagged Deal Review</h5>\n            <p>Properties with scores below 40 require:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Mandatory Success Team review before investor presentation</li>\n              <li>Documentation of why the deal is being considered despite low score</li>\n              <li>Explicit disclosure of risks to interested investors</li>\n              <li>Approval from Success Team Lead for marketplace listing</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>3. ML Feedback Obligations</h5>\n            <p>Help improve Penny by providing feedback:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Submit actual performance data for live properties</li>\n              <li>Flag inaccurate predictions within 30 days</li>\n              <li>Rate score accuracy after 90 days of operation</li>\n              <li>Document edge cases and unusual situations</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>4. Confidentiality Requirements</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Internal scoring methodology is confidential</li>\n              <li>Don't share detailed algorithm information externally</li>\n              <li>Protect ML training data and feedback</li>\n              <li>SOP verification details are staff-only</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Ethical Guidelines</h5>\n            \n            <h5>1. Prohibited Actions</h5>\n            <div class="alert-critical">\n              <strong>Never:</strong><br/>\n              • Manipulate property data to inflate scores<br/>\n              • Present AI scores as guaranteed outcomes<br/>\n              • Hide low scores from investors<br/>\n              • Override AI warnings without documentation<br/>\n              • Use AI to discriminate against investor groups\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>2. Required Actions</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Disclose AI involvement in recommendations</li>\n              <li>Explain score methodology when asked</li>\n              <li>Report AI errors or biases immediately</li>\n              <li>Maintain human oversight of all AI decisions</li>\n              <li>Document any AI overrides with justification</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>3. Continuous Learning</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Stay updated on Penny feature releases</li>\n              <li>Attend AI training sessions</li>\n              <li>Share insights from AI interactions with team</li>\n              <li>Contribute to best practices documentation</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Accountability</h5>\n            <p>Remember: You are accountable for recommendations you make, even when supported by AI. Penny provides data and analysis, but the responsibility for investor guidance remains with the Success Team.</p>\n          	5	f	2026-02-01 19:04:20.977182+00	2026-02-01 19:04:20.94+00	System	1	Initial creation - Penny AI SOPs
45c97677-635b-4b55-8d40-d17719546912	Setup_Manager	Furniture Procurement	Furniture Procurement Process	\n            <h4>Furniture Procurement & Vendor Management</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the procurement of furniture and supplies for property setups.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Approved Vendors</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Primary:</strong> Wayfair Professional, Amazon Business</li>\n              <li><strong>Secondary:</strong> IKEA, Target, HomeGoods</li>\n              <li><strong>Specialty:</strong> Local furniture rental companies</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Procurement Process</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Review property measurements and layout</li>\n              <li>Create furniture plan based on property size</li>\n              <li>Get quotes from approved vendors</li>\n              <li>Submit purchase request for approval</li>\n              <li>Place orders with confirmed delivery dates</li>\n              <li>Track all shipments and deliveries</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>Budget Guidelines</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Studio: $3,000-$5,000</li>\n              <li>1 Bedroom: $5,000-$7,000</li>\n              <li>2 Bedroom: $7,000-$10,000</li>\n              <li>3+ Bedroom: $10,000-$15,000</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Inventory Tracking</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Log all items in inventory system</li>\n              <li>Include photos, receipts, and warranty info</li>\n              <li>Track item condition over time</li>\n              <li>Schedule replacement for worn items</li>\n            </ul>\n          	2	f	2026-01-30 15:21:20.186092+00	2026-01-30 15:21:20.147+00	System	1	Initial creation
09a037d1-3999-4e9a-8a15-f297f0b7cf1b	Setup_Manager	Setup Workflow	DFY vs DIY Package Differences	<h4>Done For You (DFY) vs Do It Yourself (DIY) Package Guide</h4><p>This SOP clarifies the differences between the two setup packages and how they affect the workflow.</p><h5>Done For You (DFY)</h5><p>The DFY package is a full-service setup where the Setup Manager and Setup Pro handle everything from sourcing to on-site placement.</p><ul><li><strong>All 8 phases apply</strong></li><li>Setup Manager sources all items</li><li>Setup Pro is assigned and travels to the property</li><li>Logistics Fee ($3,350) is collected</li><li>Pro handles on-site receiving, assembly, and placement</li><li>Pro completes maintenance inventory check</li><li>Pro captures final photos and video walkthrough</li><li>Manager handles all vendor scheduling</li></ul><h5>Do It Yourself (DIY)</h5><p>The DIY package provides the Operator with the sourcing spreadsheet and guidance, but the Operator handles their own setup.</p><ul><li><strong>Phases 4, 6, and 7 are skipped</strong></li><li>No Setup Pro is assigned</li><li>No Logistics Fee is collected</li><li>Operator receives the sourcing spreadsheet</li><li>Operator handles their own purchasing and setup</li><li>Operator is responsible for their own photos/video</li><li>Setup Manager still provides guidance and support</li></ul><h5>Phase Flow Comparison</h5><p><strong>DFY:</strong> Phase 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5 → 6 → 7 → 8</p><p><strong>DIY:</strong> Phase 1 → 2 → 3 → 5 → 8 (Phases 4, 6, 7 skipped)</p><div class='alert-info'><strong>Determining Package Type:</strong> The package type is determined during the Phase 2 consultation call. The Setup Manager should clearly explain both options, their costs, and what the Operator is responsible for in each scenario. Document the decision in the portal before sending the recap.</div><h5>When to Recommend DFY</h5><ul><li>First-time operators with no setup experience</li><li>Operators who live far from the property</li><li>Properties that need significant furnishing</li><li>Operators with limited time availability</li></ul><h5>When to Recommend DIY</h5><ul><li>Experienced operators who have done setups before</li><li>Operators who live near the property</li><li>Operators who want to save on logistics costs</li><li>Properties that need minimal furnishing</li></ul>	3	f	2026-03-05 17:48:30.76482+00	2026-03-05 17:48:30.598+00	System	1	Initial creation
2b12a023-3123-47f2-b9bf-d88428c7e2cc	Success_Team	Marketplace Maintenance	Marketplace Deal Management	\n            <h4>Marketplace Deal Management Protocol</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the management of deals on the investor marketplace.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Deal Classification</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>AYP Approved Deals:</strong> Sourced and vetted by AYP team ($2,500-$12,000)</li>\n              <li><strong>Third-Party Seller Deals:</strong> Independent listings (capped at $15,000)</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Deal Verification Requirements</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Property photos (minimum 10, including exterior)</li>\n              <li>Market analysis with ADR, ARR, and occupancy data</li>\n              <li>Landlord approval confirmation</li>\n              <li>Lease terms documentation</li>\n              <li>Setup cost estimate</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>First Right of Refusal</h5>\n            <div class="alert-info">\n              <strong>24-Hour Window:</strong> When an investor submits an acquisition request and it is approved, they receive a 24-hour first right of refusal to secure the deal.\n            </div>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Send notification immediately upon approval</li>\n              <li>Set 24-hour countdown timer</li>\n              <li>Send reminder at 4 hours remaining</li>\n              <li>Release to marketplace if not claimed</li>\n            </ul>\n          	4	f	2026-01-30 15:21:19.368149+00	2026-01-30 15:21:19.331+00	System	1	Initial creation
c5cede38-9c24-47a5-957b-29569f4e880f	Success_Team	Penny AI	Maximizing Penny AI for Deal Sourcing	\n            <h4>Best Practices: Leveraging Penny AI for Optimal Results</h4>\n            <p>This SOP provides strategies and techniques for maximizing the value of Penny AI in deal sourcing and investor success.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Deal Sourcing Optimization</h5>\n            \n            <h5>1. Pre-Screening with Penny</h5>\n            <p>Use Penny to efficiently filter deals:</p>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Run batch scoring on new property lists</li>\n              <li>Sort by Penny Score to prioritize review</li>\n              <li>Focus detailed analysis on scores 60+</li>\n              <li>Quick-reject scores below 30 (unless special circumstances)</li>\n              <li>Flag 30-60 scores for secondary review</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>2. Market Timing</h5>\n            <p>Leverage seasonality data for better deals:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Check seasonality calendar before pricing discussions</li>\n              <li>Negotiate harder during low-demand months</li>\n              <li>Prioritize deals in markets entering peak season</li>\n              <li>Use ADR multipliers to project realistic revenue</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>3. Strategy Selection</h5>\n            <p>Let Penny guide operation strategy:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Review "Best Strategy" recommendation for each property</li>\n              <li>Compare revenue projections across all three strategies</li>\n              <li>Consider hybrid approaches when scores are close</li>\n              <li>Factor in investor preferences and experience level</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Investor Matching Excellence</h5>\n            \n            <h5>1. Preference Optimization</h5>\n            <p>Help investors set effective preferences:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Recommend realistic Penny Score minimums (70+ for beginners)</li>\n              <li>Suggest 3-5 target markets for better matching</li>\n              <li>Set appropriate budget ranges with 20% buffer</li>\n              <li>Review and update preferences quarterly</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>2. Proactive Matching</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Run manual matches for VIP investors weekly</li>\n              <li>Alert investors to exceptional deals (85+ scores) immediately</li>\n              <li>Create "deal alerts" for specific criteria</li>\n              <li>Track match-to-close conversion rates</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>3. Score-Based Conversations</h5>\n            <div class="alert-info">\n              <strong>Conversation Starters by Score:</strong><br/>\n              • <strong>85+:</strong> "Penny identified an exceptional opportunity..."<br/>\n              • <strong>70-84:</strong> "This deal scores well across all factors..."<br/>\n              • <strong>60-69:</strong> "Solid opportunity with some considerations..."<br/>\n              • <strong>Below 60:</strong> "I want to be transparent about the risks..."\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>Advanced Techniques</h5>\n            \n            <h5>1. Score Trend Analysis</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Track how scores change over time for saved deals</li>\n              <li>Identify deals with improving scores (market momentum)</li>\n              <li>Flag deals with declining scores for review</li>\n              <li>Use trends to time investor outreach</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>2. Component Score Deep Dives</h5>\n            <p>When overall score is borderline, analyze components:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>High financial, low regulation = permit risk worth investigating</li>\n              <li>High market, low competition = emerging opportunity</li>\n              <li>Low seasonality = consider MTR strategy instead</li>\n              <li>High location, low financial = negotiate harder on rent</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>3. Comparative Analysis</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Compare similar properties across markets</li>\n              <li>Identify why one scores higher than another</li>\n              <li>Use comparisons to educate investors</li>\n              <li>Build market expertise through pattern recognition</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>4. Risk Mitigation Strategies</h5>\n            <p>Use Penny's risk analysis proactively:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Address identified risks before investor questions</li>\n              <li>Prepare mitigation plans for common risks</li>\n              <li>Document risk acceptance for flagged deals</li>\n              <li>Use risks as negotiation leverage with landlords</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Performance Tracking</h5>\n            \n            <h5>1. Key Metrics to Monitor</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Average Penny Score of closed deals</li>\n              <li>Score accuracy (predicted vs actual performance)</li>\n              <li>Match-to-inquiry conversion rate</li>\n              <li>Time from match to close by score range</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>2. Feedback Loop</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Submit performance data for all live properties</li>\n              <li>Flag scoring errors within 30 days</li>\n              <li>Share insights in team meetings</li>\n              <li>Contribute to model improvement</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <div class="alert-warning">\n              <strong>Remember:</strong> Penny is most effective when combined with your market expertise and investor relationships. Use AI to enhance your capabilities, not replace your judgment.\n            </div>\n      