7a421d7f-afb5-4f73-ae4d-5268e3dc035e	Success_Team	Penny AI	Navigating the Penny AI Dashboard	\n            <h4>Staff Dashboard: Penny AI Navigation Guide</h4>\n            <p>This SOP provides step-by-step instructions for navigating and utilizing Penny AI features within the Staff Dashboard.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Accessing Penny AI Features</h5>\n            <p>Penny AI is integrated throughout the staff dashboard in multiple locations:</p>\n            \n            <h5>1. Deal Flow Tab - Property Cards</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Each property card displays the <strong>Penny Score Badge</strong> in the top-right corner</li>\n              <li>Color coding: Green (80+), Yellow (60-79), Orange (40-59), Red (below 40)</li>\n              <li>Click the badge to view detailed analysis</li>\n              <li>Properties with scores below 40 show a warning flag icon</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>2. Property Detail Modal - Penny Tab</h5>\n            <p>When viewing a property's details, click the "Penny AI" tab to access:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Score Header:</strong> Large score display with recommendation badge</li>\n              <li><strong>Best Strategy:</strong> Recommended operation type (STR, Co-living, or MTR)</li>\n              <li><strong>Score Breakdown:</strong> Individual scores for all 6 components</li>\n              <li><strong>Revenue Projections:</strong> Estimated monthly/annual revenue by strategy</li>\n              <li><strong>Risks & Opportunities:</strong> AI-identified factors affecting the deal</li>\n              <li><strong>SOP Checklist:</strong> Verification status for each data point (Staff Only)</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>3. SOP Verification Checklist</h5>\n            <div class="alert-info">\n              <strong>Staff-Only Feature:</strong> The SOP Checklist shows which data points Penny verified:<br/>\n              • Hotel Occupancy ✓<br/>\n              • Hotel ADR ✓<br/>\n              • STR Performance ✓<br/>\n              • Travel Trends ✓<br/>\n              • Co-Living Data ✓<br/>\n              • Regulations ✓<br/>\n              • Seasonality ✓<br/>\n              • Competition ✓\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>4. Running a New Analysis</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Open the property detail modal</li>\n              <li>Navigate to the "Penny AI" tab</li>\n              <li>Click the <strong>Refresh</strong> button to generate a new score</li>\n              <li>Wait for analysis to complete (typically 5-10 seconds)</li>\n              <li>Review updated scores and recommendations</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>5. Penny Accuracy Reports</h5>\n            <p>Access via Analytics Dashboard → Penny Accuracy:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>View prediction accuracy over time</li>\n              <li>Compare predicted vs actual revenue</li>\n              <li>Identify scoring model improvements needed</li>\n              <li>Submit feedback for ML training</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>6. ML Feedback Dashboard</h5>\n            <p>Help improve Penny's accuracy by providing feedback:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Rate score accuracy after property goes live</li>\n              <li>Flag incorrect predictions for review</li>\n              <li>Submit actual performance data for training</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <div class="alert-warning">\n              <strong>Score Expiration:</strong> Penny scores expire after 7 days. Always refresh scores for deals that have been sitting in the pipeline.\n            </div>\n          	2	f	2026-02-01 19:04:20.574735+00	2026-02-01 19:04:20.534+00	System	1	Initial creation - Penny AI SOPs
85daec86-4a09-4363-8758-b89d6aa2d59c	Success_Team	Penny AI	Penny AI & Investor Relationships	\n            <h4>Penny AI's Role in Investor Experience</h4>\n            <p>This SOP defines how Penny AI interacts with investors and the Success Team's responsibilities in managing this relationship.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Investor-Facing Penny Features</h5>\n            \n            <h5>1. Penny Chat (Investor Portal)</h5>\n            <p>Investors can chat with Penny directly through their portal:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Market Questions:</strong> "What's the outlook for Austin?"</li>\n              <li><strong>Deal Inquiries:</strong> "What deals match my preferences?"</li>\n              <li><strong>Strategy Advice:</strong> "Should I do STR or co-living?"</li>\n              <li><strong>Seasonality Info:</strong> "When is peak season in Tampa?"</li>\n              <li><strong>Regulation Updates:</strong> "Any new STR rules in Denver?"</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>2. Penny Score Visibility</h5>\n            <p>Investors see Penny Scores on:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Marketplace deal cards</li>\n              <li>Saved deals list</li>\n              <li>Deal detail pages</li>\n              <li>Quick view modals</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <div class="alert-warning">\n              <strong>What Investors DON'T See:</strong><br/>\n              • SOP verification checklist<br/>\n              • Internal risk assessments<br/>\n              • ML feedback data<br/>\n              • Accuracy reports<br/>\n              • Score calculation details\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>3. Deal Match Preferences</h5>\n            <p>Investors can set preferences that Penny uses for matching:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Target markets (multiple selections)</li>\n              <li>Budget range (min/max)</li>\n              <li>Property types (STR, Co-living, MTR)</li>\n              <li>Minimum Penny Score threshold</li>\n              <li>Bedroom requirements</li>\n              <li>Must-have features</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>4. Automated Notifications</h5>\n            <p>Penny sends notifications when:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>A new deal matches investor preferences</li>\n              <li>A saved deal's score changes significantly</li>\n              <li>Market conditions change in target markets</li>\n              <li>Regulatory updates affect their investments</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Success Team Responsibilities</h5>\n            \n            <h5>1. Score Interpretation Support</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Help investors understand what scores mean</li>\n              <li>Explain why certain deals score higher/lower</li>\n              <li>Provide context beyond the numbers</li>\n              <li>Address concerns about low-scoring deals</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>2. Managing Expectations</h5>\n            <div class="alert-info">\n              <strong>Key Talking Points:</strong><br/>\n              • Penny scores are advisory, not guarantees<br/>\n              • Scores are based on available data at time of analysis<br/>\n              • Market conditions can change after scoring<br/>\n              • Human due diligence is still essential<br/>\n              • Low scores don't mean "bad" - they indicate higher risk\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>3. Handling Score Disputes</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Listen to investor's concerns about the score</li>\n              <li>Review the score breakdown with them</li>\n              <li>Explain which factors impacted the score</li>\n              <li>If valid concerns, request a manual re-score</li>\n              <li>Document feedback for ML improvement</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>4. When Penny is Wrong</h5>\n            <p>If Penny's assessment proves inaccurate:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Acknowledge the discrepancy professionally</li>\n              <li>Submit feedback through ML dashboard</li>\n              <li>Document the case for model improvement</li>\n              <li>Never blame Penny - take ownership as a team</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>5. Escalation Protocol</h5>\n            <p>Escalate to Success Team Lead when:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Investor disputes a score and requests human review</li>\n              <li>Penny provides inconsistent information</li>\n              <li>Technical issues affect investor experience</li>\n              <li>Investor expresses distrust in AI recommendations</li>\n            </ul>\n          	4	f	2026-02-01 19:04:20.847426+00	2026-02-01 19:04:20.807+00	System	1	Initial creation - Penny AI SOPs
55eb4eba-0729-4b81-8523-0e97e8f925d0	Setup_Manager	Setup Workflow	DFY & DIY Recap Email Templates	<h1>DFY &amp; DIY Recap Email Templates</h1>\n<h2>Overview</h2>\n<p>After the consultation call (Phase 2), the Setup Manager sends a recap email to the Operator outlining their chosen package, fee structure, and next steps. The portal provides two automated templates — one for <strong>Done For You (DFY)</strong> and one for <strong>Do It Yourself (DIY)</strong> — that auto-populate with project-specific data.</p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>How to Send a Recap</h2>\n<h3>From the Setup Project Detail:</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Open the project and go to <strong>Phase 2 Actions</strong> or the <strong>Recap Templates</strong> tab.</li>\n<li>Select the package type (DFY or DIY) if not already set.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>"Compose &amp; Send Recap"</strong> to open the template editor.</li>\n<li>Review and edit the template variables:\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Client Name</strong> — Auto-filled from operator name</li>\n<li><strong># Properties</strong> — Number of properties being set up</li>\n<li><strong>Beds / Baths</strong> — Property bedroom and bathroom count</li>\n<li><strong>Property Type</strong> — Apartment, house, condo, etc.</li>\n<li><strong>City, State</strong> — Auto-extracted from property address</li>\n<li><strong>Target Start Date</strong> — When the operator wants to go live</li>\n<li><strong>Setup Manager Name</strong> — Your name (auto-filled)</li>\n<li><strong>Intake Form Link</strong> — Link to the intake form</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Preview the email using the <strong>"Email Preview"</strong> button to see the exact HTML email.</li>\n<li>Send via <strong>Email</strong> (to operator's email) or <strong>Portal Message</strong> (to their portal inbox).</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Quick Copy:</h3>\n<p>Use the <strong>"Copy Text"</strong> button to copy the plain-text version for pasting into other messaging platforms (WhatsApp, SMS, etc.).</p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>Template: Done For You (DFY)</h2>\n<p><strong>Subject:</strong> Recap &amp; Next Steps: Setting up your property!</p>\n<p><strong>Email includes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Property recap (# properties, beds, baths, type, location, start date)</li>\n<li><strong>Three fee line items:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Administration Team fee (with Paid/Pending status)</li>\n<li>On-the-Ground Setup Team and logistics: $3,350</li>\n<li>Furniture Package Fee (variable, based on selections)</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Four-step process:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Fill out the Intake Form (link provided)</li>\n<li>Sign service agreement + pay setup &amp; logistics fee</li>\n<li>Product sourcing (24-48 hrs) → spreadsheet → furniture fee → purchase</li>\n<li>On-the-ground team receives, unboxes, assembles, sets up Wi-Fi, takes photos, handles cleanup (7-14 business days)</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>Payment info (Zelle to admin@cooperfamilyinc.net)</li>\n<li>Website link (accessyourplace.com)</li>\n<li>Manager signature</li>\n</ul>\n<hr/>\n<h2>Template: Do It Yourself (DIY)</h2>\n<p><strong>Subject:</strong> Recap &amp; Next Steps: Setting up your property!</p>\n<p><strong>Email includes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Property recap (# properties, beds, baths, type, location, start date)</li>\n<li><strong>Two fee line items:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Administration Team fee (with Paid/Pending status)</li>\n<li>Furniture Package Fee (variable, based on selections)</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Four-step process:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Fill out the Intake Form (link provided)</li>\n<li>Sign service agreement</li>\n<li>Product sourcing (24-48 hrs) → spreadsheet → furniture fee → purchase</li>\n<li><strong>Operator's team</strong> receives, unboxes, assembles, sets up Wi-Fi, takes photos, handles cleanup (7-14 business days)</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>Payment info (Zelle to admin@cooperfamilyinc.net)</li>\n<li>Website link (accessyourplace.com)</li>\n<li>Manager signature</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Key Differences from DFY:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>No $3,350 logistics fee</strong> line item</li>\n<li>Step 2 says "signed" only (no logistics fee mention)</li>\n<li>Step 4 says "Your on-the-ground setup team" instead of "Our"</li>\n<li>Step 4 says "You'll also handle property photos and any cleanup" instead of "We'll also handle"</li>\n</ul>\n<hr/>\n<h2>Template Variable Reference</h2>\n<table border="1" cellpadding="8" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%">\n<thead><tr style="background:#f0f0f0"><th>Variable</th><th>Source</th><th>Fallback</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Client Name</td><td>investor_name</td><td>"there"</td></tr>\n<tr><td># Properties</td><td>num_properties</td><td>1</td></tr>\n<tr><td># Beds</td><td>num_beds</td><td>"[beds]"</td></tr>\n<tr><td># Baths</td><td>num_baths</td><td>"[baths]"</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Property Type</td><td>property_type</td><td>"apartment"</td></tr>\n<tr><td>City, State</td><td>city_state</td><td>Extracted from address</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Start Date</td><td>target_start_date</td><td>"[Date TBD]"</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Admin Fee</td><td>admin_fee_amount</td><td>$2,500</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Admin Status</td><td>admin_fee_paid</td><td>"Pending Payment"</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Manager Name</td><td>assigned_manager_name</td><td>"Your Setup Manager"</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Intake Link</td><td>intake_form_link</td><td>Portal URL</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr/>\n<h2>Delivery Methods</h2>\n<h3>1. Email (Primary)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Sends a professionally styled HTML email via Resend</li>\n<li>Includes both HTML and plain-text versions</li>\n<li>Recipient: operator's email on file</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. Portal Message (Secondary)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Sends as an in-portal message to the operator's notification center</li>\n<li>Uses plain-text format</li>\n<li>Requires operator to have a portal account</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. Copy to Clipboard</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Copies the plain-text version for manual sending via WhatsApp, SMS, or other channels</li>\n</ul>\n<hr/>\n<h2>After Sending</h2>\n<p>When a recap is sent:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The project's recap_sent flag is set to true</li>\n<li>The recap_sent_at timestamp is recorded</li>\n<li>The recap_type (dfy/diy) is saved</li>\n<li>The plain-text body is stored in recap_email_body for reference</li>\n<li>All template variables are saved back to the project</li>\n<li>An activity log entry is created</li>\n<li>The recap can be resent at any time with updated variables</li>\n</ol>\n<hr/>\n<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>\n<table border="1" cellpadding="8" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%">\n<thead><tr style="background:#f0f0f0"><th>Issue</th><th>Solution</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>"No Email" error</td><td>Add operator email in project settings</td></tr>\n<tr><td>"No Portal Account" error</td><td>Operator needs to register; use email instead</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Variables showing brackets</td><td>Fill in missing fields in the template editor</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Email not received</td><td>Check spam folder; verify email address; check Resend logs</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Need to resend</td><td>Click "View / Resend Recap" — all previous data is preserved</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><em>Last updated: March 2026 | Version: 1.0</em></p>	0	f	2026-03-05 18:04:45.510516+00	2026-03-05 18:04:45.510516+00	System	1	Initial creation of DFY & DIY Recap Email Templates SOP
3c1cb7e8-1e66-4bfe-9c25-0e6388c5a5d1	Cross_Team	Communication Standards	Communication Standards & Guidelines	\n            <h4>Communication Standards & Professional Guidelines</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs all internal and external communications.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Investor Communication</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Always professional and courteous tone</li>\n              <li>Respond within 4 business hours</li>\n              <li>Use approved email templates when available</li>\n              <li>Document all communications in CRM</li>\n              <li>Escalate concerns to Success Team if needed</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Landlord Communication</h5>\n            <div class="alert-critical">\n              <strong>Ocean307 Protocol:</strong> Always identify yourself with the company password when contacting landlords.\n            </div>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Professional and respectful at all times</li>\n              <li>Clear and concise messaging</li>\n              <li>Follow up as promised</li>\n              <li>Document all interactions</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Internal Communication</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Use staff messaging for team coordination</li>\n              <li>Keep CRM notes updated</li>\n              <li>Attend required team meetings</li>\n              <li>Share relevant updates promptly</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Prohibited Actions</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Sharing confidential information externally</li>\n              <li>Making commitments outside your authority</li>\n              <li>Negative comments about AYP or team members</li>\n              <li>Unauthorized contact with landlords (investors)</li>\n            </ul>\n          	2	f	2026-01-30 15:21:20.684608+00	2026-01-30 15:21:20.645+00	System	1	Initial creation
57472629-b8ae-446d-a684-525e7ca260e3	Cross_Team	Cross-Team Handoffs	Cross-Team Handoff Protocol	\n            <h4>Cross-Team Handoff & Communication Protocol</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs communication and handoffs between teams.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Handoff Triggers</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Acquisition → Success:</strong> Deal approved and investor matched</li>\n              <li><strong>Success → Setup:</strong> Lease signed and move-in date confirmed</li>\n              <li><strong>Setup → Success:</strong> Property launch complete</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Handoff Requirements</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Complete all documentation in CRM</li>\n              <li>Update deal status to reflect handoff</li>\n              <li>Send handoff notification to receiving team</li>\n              <li>Schedule handoff call if needed</li>\n              <li>Confirm receipt and understanding</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Communication Channels</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Urgent:</strong> Phone call or SMS</li>\n              <li><strong>Standard:</strong> Staff messaging system</li>\n              <li><strong>Documentation:</strong> CRM notes and updates</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Response Time Standards</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Urgent issues: 30 minutes</li>\n              <li>Standard requests: 4 hours</li>\n              <li>Non-urgent updates: 24 hours</li>\n            </ul>\n          	1	f	2026-01-30 15:21:20.57441+00	2026-01-30 15:21:20.524+00	System	1	Initial creation
19396c64-1821-4d1e-8288-5933b47ce9d9	Success_Team	Dispute Resolution	III. Dispute Resolution & Escalation	<h4>Dispute Resolution & Escalation</h4>\n<p>To maintain professional boundaries and record-keeping, all conflicts must follow the official escalation path.</p>\n<h5>The Dispute Tab</h5>\n<p>If a client has a technical issue, vendor dispute, or operational conflict, AMs and SMs must direct the client to submit a formal ticket via the <strong>Dispute Tab</strong> in the investor portal.</p>\n<h5>ST Resolution</h5>\n<p>The Success Team is responsible for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Reviewing escalations</li>\n<li>Gathering data from the relevant department</li>\n<li>Facilitating a resolution</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Platform Neutrality</h5>\n<p>As per the Integrity Standard, ST will <strong>not intervene</strong> in disputes arising from services offered by staff members outside the official scope of Access Your Place.</p>\n<div class="alert-warning">\n<strong>Important:</strong> Always direct clients to the Dispute Tab for formal tracking. Do not attempt to resolve disputes through informal channels.\n</div>	3	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
05313d50-ecd4-4e4c-aef4-750285051f6c	Success_Team	Onboarding	I. Discovery & Onboarding Bridge	<h4>The Discovery & Onboarding Bridge</h4>\n<p>The Success Team (ST) manages the administrative flow while supporting Acquisition Managers (AM) in the initial discovery phase.</p>\n<h5>Consultative Capital Gauge</h5>\n<p>During initial discovery calls, AMs use a <strong>$5,000 capital availability marker</strong> as a consultative gauge to assess an investor's readiness. This is <em>not a rigid barrier</em> but a discovery tool to ensure the client is positioned for a successful launch.</p>\n<h5>Account Initiation</h5>\n<p>AMs must encourage all clients to create their free account on the Access Your Place platform to track their acquisitions and access the resource library.</p>\n<h5>Initial Dispatch</h5>\n<p>Upon AM confirmation of a deal, ST sends the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Welcome Email</li>\n<li>Terms of Service</li>\n<li>Payment Instructions</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Verification</h5>\n<p>ST verifies funds via <strong>Zelle: Admin@cooperfamilyinc.net</strong> and dispatches the Congratulations Packet including:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Acquisition Agreement</li>\n<li>Corporate Application</li>\n</ul>\n<div class="alert-info">\n<strong>Key Point:</strong> The $5,000 capital marker is a consultative gauge during AM discovery calls, not a hard block for platform access.\n</div>	1	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
1706e6e1-904e-4dd8-ae00-015f89a0ca7a	Success_Team	Setup Management	II. Setup Management & Logistics Bridge	<h4>Setup Management & Logistics Bridge</h4>\n<p>The ST serves as the logistical backbone for the Setup Management Department to ensure turn-key launches.</p>\n<h5>Sourcing & Tracking</h5>\n<p>ST collaborates with Setup Managers (SM) to source all furniture/decor through approved suppliers and assists with ordering and tracking all items.</p>\n<h5>Financial Records</h5>\n<p>ST generates the inventory spreadsheets for SM review and secures final client confirmation on project costs.</p>\n<h5>Vendor Repository</h5>\n<p>ST maintains a secure depository of verified vendors for SM use:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Housekeepers</li>\n<li>Photographers</li>\n<li>Junk removal vendors</li>\n</ul>\n<div class="alert-info">\n<strong>Coordination:</strong> All vendor communications should be documented in the property notes for audit trail purposes.\n</div>	2	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
d1a6dd0a-9c5a-4d6c-ae15-cf870b4752c2	Acquisition_Manager	Deal Negotiation	Deal Negotiation Standards	\n            <h4>Deal Negotiation & Terms Structuring</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the negotiation process and standard deal terms.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Standard Lease Terms</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Lease duration: 12-24 months (preferred)</li>\n              <li>Rent: Market rate or below</li>\n              <li>Security deposit: 1-2 months rent</li>\n              <li>Subletting clause: Must allow corporate subletting</li>\n              <li>Furnishing: Permission to furnish the unit</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Negotiation Guidelines</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Start with standard terms, adjust based on landlord needs</li>\n              <li>Emphasize guaranteed income and professional management</li>\n              <li>Be prepared to offer longer lease for better terms</li>\n              <li>Never commit to terms outside your authority</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <div class="alert-warning">\n              <strong>Half-Funded Rule:</strong> Full property address is disclosed only after 50% of the acquisition fee is funded or the investor has closed a prior deal with AYP.\n            </div>\n            \n            <h5>Deal Approval Process</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Complete property analysis and documentation</li>\n              <li>Submit deal for Success Team review</li>\n              <li>Receive approval or feedback within 24 hours</li>\n              <li>Proceed with investor presentation if approved</li>\n            </ol>\n          	3	f	2026-01-30 15:21:19.704825+00	2026-01-30 15:21:19.658+00	System	1	Initial creation
308037d8-2aaa-481c-825b-474fd35b9472	Cross_Team	Communication Standards	Ocean307 Security Protocol	<h4>Ocean307 Security Protocol</h4>\n<p>All staff must use this verification protocol when contacting landlords, property managers, or vendor partners.</p>\n<h5>When to Use</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial contact with any landlord or property manager</li>\n<li>Vendor coordination calls</li>\n<li>Partner verification requests</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Protocol</h5>\n<p>Lead with: "This is [Your Name] from Access Your Place. Our verification code is <strong>Ocean307</strong>."</p>\n<div class="alert-critical">\n<strong>Critical:</strong> This protocol protects our network. Failure to use it may result in partners refusing to work with you.\n</div>	1	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
cea9ed61-e40d-4398-9894-48c426bc3529	Acquisition_Manager	Consultative Framework	AM: Expert Guidance Principle	<h4>Expert Guidance Principle</h4>\n<p>Acquisition Managers serve as expert guides, not salespeople. Your role is to help investors make informed decisions about rental arbitrage opportunities.</p>\n<h5>Consultative Approach</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Listen to investor goals and constraints</li>\n<li>Assess capital readiness using the $5,000 gauge</li>\n<li>Provide honest market analysis</li>\n<li>Never pressure clients into deals</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Capital Assessment</h5>\n<p>The <strong>$5,000 capital availability marker</strong> is a consultative gauge to assess readiness, not a rigid barrier. Use it during discovery calls to ensure clients are positioned for success.</p>\n<div class="alert-info">\n<strong>Remember:</strong> Your success is measured by client success, not transaction volume.\n</div>	1	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
a26e3693-69ee-4ccb-9b97-6818bcbf9c78	Acquisition_Manager	Deal Negotiation	AM: Half-Funded Rule	<h4>Half-Funded Rule</h4>\n<p>To protect our landlord network and maintain deal integrity, full property addresses are disclosed only under specific conditions.</p>\n<h5>Address Disclosure Requirements</h5>\n<p>Full property address is disclosed <strong>ONLY</strong> when:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>50% of acquisition fee is funded, OR</li>\n<li>Client has successfully closed a prior deal with AYP</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Before Half-Funding</h5>\n<p>You may share:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>General area/neighborhood</li>\n<li>Property type and specifications</li>\n<li>Rental projections and market data</li>\n<li>Photos (with address obscured)</li>\n</ul>\n<div class="alert-warning">\n<strong>Warning:</strong> Disclosing full addresses before half-funding violates company policy and may result in disciplinary action.\n</div>	2	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
a746843f-9628-4a38-9c61-81b076a34f2e	Acquisition_Manager	Property Research	AM: Research Responsibility	<h4>Research Responsibility</h4>\n<p>AMs are responsible for thorough market research before presenting any deal to investors.</p>\n<h5>Required Data Sources</h5>\n<p>Cross-reference the following platforms for validation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AirDNA</strong> - ADR, occupancy rates</li>\n<li><strong>Rabbu</strong> - Market comparables</li>\n<li><strong>Mashvisor</strong> - Investment analysis</li>\n<li><strong>AllTheRooms</strong> - Competitive landscape</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Validation Metrics</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Average Daily Rate (ADR)</li>\n<li>Annual Revenue Rate (ARR)</li>\n<li>Occupancy percentage</li>\n<li>Seasonal variations</li>\n</ul>\n<div class="alert-info">\n<strong>Best Practice:</strong> Document all research findings in the deal notes for transparency and audit purposes.\n</div>	3	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
fef180a9-36f4-4d4c-94ef-b1a27143dd49	Setup_Manager	Property Preparation	SM: Mood Board Creation	<h4>Mood Board Creation</h4>\n<p>Every property setup begins with a mood board that guides the entire design direction.</p>\n<h5>Mood Board Requirements</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Property photos and layout</li>\n<li>Target guest demographic</li>\n<li>Color palette selection</li>\n<li>Furniture style direction</li>\n<li>Budget allocation breakdown</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Client Approval</h5>\n<p>Mood board must be approved by the investor before any purchases are made.</p>\n<div class="alert-info">\n<strong>Tip:</strong> Include 2-3 style options to give investors choice while maintaining design coherence.\n</div>	1	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
61400425-a574-42ac-9ed5-384a56ef02fe	Setup_Manager	Furniture Procurement	SM: Inventory Management	<h4>Inventory Management</h4>\n<p>Proper inventory tracking ensures budget adherence and accountability.</p>\n<h5>Inventory Spreadsheet Requirements</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Item description and quantity</li>\n<li>Vendor and purchase link</li>\n<li>Unit cost and total cost</li>\n<li>Delivery status and ETA</li>\n<li>Installation notes</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Budget Tracking</h5>\n<p>Update the inventory spreadsheet in real-time as purchases are made. Flag any items that exceed budget estimates immediately.</p>\n<div class="alert-warning">\n<strong>Important:</strong> All purchases over $500 require investor pre-approval.\n</div>	2	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
9ad2102c-fcc8-4b00-a633-c281d4d0f23a	Setup_Manager	Vendor Management	SM: YP Pro Coordination	<h4>YP Pro Coordination</h4>\n<p>Coordinate with verified vendors (YP Pros) for professional services.</p>\n<h5>Vendor Categories</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Photographers - Listing photos</li>\n<li>Housekeepers - Initial deep clean</li>\n<li>Handymen - Minor repairs and assembly</li>\n<li>Junk removal - Pre-setup clearing</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Vendor Verification</h5>\n<p>Only use vendors from the ST-maintained vendor repository. If a new vendor is needed, submit for approval before engagement.</p>\n<div class="alert-info">\n<strong>Protocol:</strong> Always use password "Ocean307" when contacting vendors on behalf of AYP.\n</div>	3	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
0f08b7fe-8d52-4261-b1c1-c910540cd41b	Setup_Manager	Quality Inspection	SM: Task Finalization	<h4>Task Finalization</h4>\n<p>Complete these steps before marking a setup as complete.</p>\n<h5>Final Checklist</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>All furniture assembled and placed</li>\n<li>Linens and amenities stocked</li>\n<li>Professional photos taken</li>\n<li>Listing created and reviewed</li>\n<li>Smart locks programmed</li>\n<li>Welcome guide printed</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Handoff to Success Team</h5>\n<p>Submit final inventory spreadsheet and photo gallery to ST for investor review and platform listing approval.</p>\n<div class="alert-info">\n<strong>Quality Check:</strong> Walk through the property as if you were a guest. Would you be satisfied with the experience?\n</div>	4	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
a8094934-1436-4687-8b18-2e35f8696b7a	Setup_Manager	Property Preparation	Property Preparation Checklist	\n            <h4>Property Preparation & Launch Checklist</h4>\n            <p>This SOP governs the preparation of properties for furnished rental operations.</p>\n            \n            <h5>Pre-Setup Assessment</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Conduct initial property walkthrough</li>\n              <li>Document existing condition with photos</li>\n              <li>Measure all rooms for furniture planning</li>\n              <li>Check all utilities and appliances</li>\n              <li>Note any repairs or maintenance needed</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Setup Timeline</h5>\n            <ol>\n              <li>Day 1-2: Deep cleaning and repairs</li>\n              <li>Day 3-5: Furniture delivery and assembly</li>\n              <li>Day 6-7: Decor, linens, and final touches</li>\n              <li>Day 8: Professional photography</li>\n              <li>Day 9: Quality inspection and listing creation</li>\n            </ol>\n            \n            <h5>Essential Items Checklist</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Bedroom: Bed frame, mattress, nightstands, dresser, linens</li>\n              <li>Living Room: Sofa, coffee table, TV, entertainment center</li>\n              <li>Kitchen: Cookware, dishes, utensils, small appliances</li>\n              <li>Bathroom: Towels, toiletries, shower curtain</li>\n              <li>General: WiFi router, smart lock, cleaning supplies</li>\n            </ul>\n            \n            <h5>Quality Standards</h5>\n            <ul>\n              <li>All furniture must be new or like-new condition</li>\n              <li>Consistent design aesthetic throughout</li>\n              <li>Hotel-quality linens and towels</li>\n              <li>Professional-grade photography required</li>\n            </ul>\n          	1	f	2026-01-30 15:21:20.076013+00	2026-01-30 15:21:20.039+00	System	1	Initial creation
e874f2f7-a6ba-4384-8fe9-3c810a73ebbd	Cross_Team	Cross-Team Handoffs	Deal Handoff Protocol	<h4>Deal Handoff Protocol</h4>\n<p>Smooth handoffs between departments ensure client satisfaction and operational efficiency.</p>\n<h5>AM to ST Handoff (Deal Confirmed)</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Investor contact information verified</li>\n<li>Deal terms documented in system</li>\n<li>Payment instructions sent</li>\n<li>ST notified via platform</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>ST to SM Handoff (Setup Ready)</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Lease signed and uploaded</li>\n<li>Keys/access arranged</li>\n<li>Budget approved by investor</li>\n<li>SM assigned and notified</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>SM to ST Handoff (Setup Complete)</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Final inventory submitted</li>\n<li>Photos uploaded</li>\n<li>Listing draft created</li>\n<li>ST review requested</li>\n</ul>\n<div class="alert-info">\n<strong>Communication:</strong> Use the platform messaging system for all handoff communications to maintain audit trail.\n</div>	2	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
4849d580-a73b-4100-b435-f84de23f426d	Cross_Team	Dispute Resolution	Dispute Escalation Path	<h4>Dispute Escalation Path</h4>\n<p>All team members must follow this escalation path for client issues.</p>\n<h5>Step 1: Direct to Dispute Tab</h5>\n<p>When a client raises an issue, provide this response:</p>\n<p><em>"To ensure your issue is tracked and resolved officially, please submit a ticket in the 'Dispute' tab of your portal."</em></p>\n<h5>Step 2: ST Review</h5>\n<p>Success Team reviews the ticket, gathers information from relevant departments, and assigns priority.</p>\n<h5>Step 3: Resolution</h5>\n<p>ST coordinates resolution and communicates outcome to all parties.</p>\n<div class="alert-warning">\n<strong>Important:</strong> Do not attempt to resolve disputes outside the official system. This protects both you and the client.\n</div>	3	f	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	2026-01-30 05:27:32.134172+00	System	1	Updated with Success Team Master SOP
